Identity provider, OAuth2/OIDC authorization server, and account-management
GraphQL API for NeoWorks (Go module `github.com/neoworks/auth`).

## Contents

- [Architecture](/docs/api/architecture) — system overview, package map, runtime
  components, identity/encryption model.
- [OAuth2 / OIDC flow](/docs/api/oauth) — authorize → login → consent → token
  exchange → refresh, end to end.
- [HTTP API reference](/docs/api/http-api) — every REST/OIDC route, request/response
  shapes, auth requirements.
- [GraphQL API](/docs/api/graphql-api) — schema, queries, mutations for Contacts,
  OAuth Clients, Client Databases, and Refresh Tokens.
- [Data model](/docs/api/data-model) — SurrealDB schema (tables, fields,
  constraints), versioning pattern, Redis/S3 layout.
- [Canonical entity surface](/docs/api/entity-surface) — the composable capability
  contract (CRUD, query/filter, soft-delete, versioning, relations, real-time,
  bulk) every entity opts into, with SurrealQL mappings and a roadmap.
- [Development & operations](/docs/api/development) — environment variables,
  running locally, migrations, GraphQL codegen, tests, conventions.

## Quick links

- GraphQL Playground: `/playground`
- OIDC discovery: `/.well-known/openid-configuration`
- JWKS: `/.well-known/jwks.json`
